063 #edb/ref 17592186110782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111774 #edb/ref 1061 9486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111774 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d10125a1-a3c4-5723-8b84-ca4ef525a806" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111774 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110783 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111783 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111784 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111783 #edb/ref 1061 9553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111783 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a10c82d4-3ea7-5197-929f-a0a7a5910276" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111783 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111784 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111784 #edb/ref 1061 9554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111784 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2fa4b989-a0cc-59a1-af0b-34fffe8e4efd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111784 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110790 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111785 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111785 #edb/ref 1061 9559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111785 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7b16a667-2831-57ad-9ccc-a74ad42b6006" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111785 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111786 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111786 #edb/ref 1061 9560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111786 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "904ecf87-997e-5efd-aa14-ee221a6d6685" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111786 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111787 #edb/ref 1061 9561 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111787 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c961c803-6d65-5690-a563-dc412e97f007" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111787 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111848 #edb/ref 1064 "A **rectangle** is a parallelogram where all angles are right. It has all the properties of parallelograms: its opposite sides are parallel and congruent.\n\n![](images/1f/1fa96b5993a48483798ff4ac05d75f1ffa271f82e5ed6e61a452eb97b3daf3e4.png)\n\nIf all $4$ sides of a rectangle are congruent, then it is a **square**.\n\n![](images/82/822788813f0e81eebef50f324e1bcaf329e7fa5552e10557a19d20b4e868063e.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111848 #edb/ref 1065 2270 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111848 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1fb26940-464f-55d2-9903-b4695c595b5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111848 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111851 #edb/ref 1064 "Two polygons are **congruent** if they have the same shape. This means that\n\n- they have the same number of sides,\n\n- all corresponding sides are congruent, and\n\n- all corresponding interior angles are congruent.\n\nConsider the two polygons $\\mathcal{P}$ and $\\mathcal{Q}$ below. Are they congruent?\n\n![](images/b0/b0a11815bf9006ccdca0ebe71ff7ba53ac7526c71a715ece71914b103b4a24a8.png)\n\nLet's check these criteria for our polygons $\\mathcal{P}$ and $\\mathcal{Q}.$ We can see that both polygons have $3$ sides, and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{AB} & ≅\\overset{―}{XY}\\,, & \\overset{―}{AC} & ≅\\overset{―}{XZ}\\,, & \\overset{―}{BC} & ≅\\overset{―}{YZ}\\,, \\\\ ∠X & ≅∠A\\,, & ∠Y & ≅∠B\\,, & ∠Z & ≅∠C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polygons are congruent, and we can write \n\n$$\nABC \\cong XYZ.\n$$\n\nThe order in which we write the symbols is important: the corresponding vertices have to be in the same order.\n\nWe can also write $\\mathcal{P} \\cong \\mathcal{Q}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111851 #edb/ref 1065 2293 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111851 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e6be6893-a7ca-578a-9510-8a8c2166e89b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111851 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111858 #edb/ref 1064 "The diagonals of a rectangle are equal and bisect each other. Consequently, they divide a rectangle into four isosceles triangles, as shown below.\n\n![](images/4f/4f0aafdf04bb7f967122fc8f90454b1b09787e375857bac3bcf5fdf80925e32c.png)\n\nIn a square, the diagonals also bisect the angles.\n\n![](images/cd/cd61fabe993fa6cde5ea4020a659e86b3543597d70a304b3e5ada3abfa426186.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111858 #edb/ref 1065 2357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111858 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "4643230c-067e-5817-af66-88717e7b8c66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111858 #edb/ref 1067 "The Diagonals of Rectangles and Squares" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
